From: s6-gamescope-nvidia worker <ai@wiltaylor.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: drop export info when importing a resource

vkAllocateMemory with VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA becomes an import of
the resource's fd (VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR), but the guest's pNext chain is
forwarded as is, so a VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo the guest chained reaches
the driver beside the import. Zink chains both whenever it imports a
dma-buf (zink_resource.c allocate_bo).

NVIDIA's Linux driver (615.78.08, RTX 5090) returns VK_SUCCESS for that
allocation but allocates new memory instead of importing: writes through
the import never reach the shared buffer, and reads see zeros. RADV
imports. It reproduces natively on the host without Venus. In a SteamOS
guest every buffer Xwayland (glamor on Zink) imports is affected, so
gamescope composited black frames (VMLabDev/vmlab#171).

Imported memory never backs a blob (only memory vkr allocates does), so the
export info has no use here. Drop it before calling the driver.
---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -261,6 +261,22 @@
    VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo *export_info =
       vkr_find_struct(alloc_info->pNext, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXPORT_MEMORY_ALLOCATE_INFO);
 
+   /* An import of an existing resource is never exported from here: the guest
+    * already holds the resource, and only memory vkr allocated itself backs a
+    * blob. Drop the guest's export info so the driver sees a plain import.
+    * NVIDIA's Linux driver (615.78) given VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR together with
+    * VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo returns VK_SUCCESS but allocates new memory
+    * instead of importing, so writes through the import never reach the shared
+    * buffer. Zink chains both when it imports a dma-buf, which left every
+    * Xwayland buffer gamescope composites black.
+    */
+   if (res_info && export_info) {
+      VkBaseInStructure *prev_of_export_info =
+         vkr_find_prev_struct(alloc_info, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXPORT_MEMORY_ALLOCATE_INFO);
+      prev_of_export_info->pNext = export_info->pNext;
+      export_info = NULL;
+   }
+
    /* track if driver has requested export allocation */
    const bool might_export = export_info && export_info->handleTypes;
 
